<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51127" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vīsĭbĭlis</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		video. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Pass.</i>, <i>that may be seen</i>,
				<i>visible</i> (late Lat. for adspectabilis):
			exhalationes tenues vixque visibiles, App. de Mundo, p. 60, 37;
				<i><span class="en">id. de Deo Socr. p. 42, 22</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">deus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Apoth. 146</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gloria,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Cath. 5, 158</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>that can see</i>, <i>seeing</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pars animi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 37, 54, § 146</span></i>
			.— <i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vīsĭbĭlĭter</span></b>  (acc.
			to I.), <i>visibly</i>, <i><span class="en">Paul.
				Nol. Ep. 20</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
